---
id: org.dxos.plugin.animator
name: AnimatorPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Animation as a capability of Composer rather than a feature of one plugin. An **Animation** is a sequence of
**shots**; each shot plays one object that another plugin owns (a canvas scene, a 3D scene) for a duration, with
properties keyed on a timeline, scripted by declarative beats, and decorated by **effects**: sandboxed, agent-written
code that draws what keys cannot (packets on links, particle bursts, conversations). Plugins that own objects
contribute a **stage** that renders them; the animator never learns their object model. Rendering is deterministic,
so playback, scrubbing and export show the same frame for the same time, and an export reaches plugin-studio as a
video clip.

The neutral engine (timelines, easing, clock, script compiler, effect runtime) lives in `@dxos/animation`, and its
timeline UI in `@dxos/react-ui-animation`; both are factored out of react-ui-canvas. The design and its reasons are
in the package's `docs/DESIGN.md`.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term         | URI                             |
|--------------|---------------------------------|
| `type`       | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`         |
| `capability` | `org.dxos.mdl.capability@1.0`   |
| `component`  | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`    |
| `op`         | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`           |
| `feat`       | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`         |
| `scenario`   | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`     |
| `decision`   | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`     |

### Existing types used by this plugin

| Type                 | Source                   | Notes                                                              |
| -------------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `Easing`, `Keyframe`, `Track`, `Timeline` | `@dxos/animation` | Moved from react-ui-canvas; tracks keyed by `${target}:${property}`. |
| `Drawing.Canvas`     | `@dxos/plugin-canvas`    | Stage object of the canvas stage.                                  |
| `Spacetime.Scene`    | `@dxos/plugin-spacetime` | Stage object of the 3D stage.                                      |
| `MediaArtifact`, `Variant` | `@dxos/plugin-studio` | Where an exported animation lands as a clip.                     |
| `GenerationService`  | `@dxos/plugin-studio`    | The provider contract the exporter implements.                     |

## Types

```mdl
type Animation
  desc: >
    A film made of shots played one after another. Each shot references the object it animates, so one Animation can
    span objects from several plugins and one object can appear in several Animations without being edited.
  typename: org.dxos.type.animator.animation
  fields:
    name?: string
    fps: number                     # export rate; playback samples by time at display rate
    size?: Size                     # export frame size in pixels
    shots: Shot[]
  annotations:
    icon: ph--film-strip--regular
    hue: violet
    label: [name]
```

```mdl
type Shot
  desc: >
    One stage object played for a duration. `timeline` holds hand-placed keys; `script` holds declarative beats the
    animator compiles to keys. Where both set the same property at the same time, the hand key wins.
  fields:
    id: string
    stage: Ref<Obj.Unknown>         # an object some Stage renders
    duration: number                # seconds
    timeline: Timeline
    script?: Beat[]
    camera?: Track                  # shape owned by the stage (2D pan/zoom, orbit)
    effects: EffectInstance[]
    transition?: Transition
    markers?: Marker[]
```

```mdl
type Beat
  desc: >
    One state in a declarative shot script. Targets are stage-local ids; `layout` names an arranger the stage
    contributes, so the script states intent and the stage computes positions.
  fields:
    at?: number                     # seconds into the shot; default: after the previous beat
    duration: number                # length of the move into this state
    ease?: Easing
    show?: string[]
    hide?: string[]
    set?: Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>   # target → property → value
    layout?: { kind: string, targets: string[], params?: Record<string, unknown> }
    merge?: { from: string[], into: string }
    camera?: Record<string, unknown>
    effects?: { add?: EffectInstance[], remove?: string[] }
    caption?: string
```

```mdl
type Transition
  fields:
    kind: cut | fade | dissolve
    duration: number
```

```mdl
type Marker
  fields:
    t: number
    label: string
    caption?: string
```

```mdl
type AnimatableKind
  desc: >
    The value kind recorded by `AnimatableAnnotation` on a schema property, which fixes how it interpolates.
    `rotation` interpolates by quaternion slerp and is stored as Euler degrees; `color` interpolates in OKLab;
    `discrete` holds until the next key.
  literals: number | point | size | vec3 | rotation | color | discrete
```

```mdl
type Effect
  desc: >
    Agent-written code that draws what keys cannot. One TypeScript module exporting a stateless `sample` or a
    stateful `init`/`step`/`draw`; compiled once per version and run in a worker with no DOM, network or space
    access, at a fixed step with seeded random, checkpoints and a per-step budget. Replaces the canvas Generator type.
  typename: org.dxos.type.animator.effect
  fields:
    name: string
    description: string
    renderer: 2d | 3d | overlay
    source: string
    params: JsonSchema              # bindings via `x-binding` (node, link, object); numeric params are animatable
    version: number
  annotations:
    icon: ph--sparkle--regular
    hue: violet
    label: [name]
```

```mdl
type EffectInstance
  fields:
    id: string
    effect: Ref<Effect>
    params: Record<string, unknown>
    seed?: number
```

```mdl
type Sample
  desc: The value of every keyed target property at one time in a shot.
  fields:
    t: number
    values: Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>   # target → property → value
    camera?: Record<string, unknown>
```

```mdl
type EffectFrame
  desc: >
    What one effect drew at one time: `Shape[]` for `2d`, `Instance3D[]` (primitive, position, scale, colour,
    opacity) for `3d`, `OverlayItem[]` (anchored bubbles, cards, lines) for `overlay`.
  fields:
    instance: string                # EffectInstance id
    renderer: 2d | 3d | overlay
    items: unknown[]
```

## Capabilities

```mdl
capability AnimatorCapabilities.Stage
  desc: |
    Contributed by a plugin that owns objects, one per stage object type. Lists the targets of a stage object and
    their animatable properties (from `AnimatableAnnotation`), names the layouts its scripts may use and the effect
    renderers it can draw, and renders the stage for a `Sample` and the frame's `EffectFrame`s. It applies samples to
    a view of its objects and never writes them to ECHO; it reports edits made at a time so the animator can key
    them, and calls `onFrameDrawn(t)` once the frame for `t` is on screen.
  type: StageDef
  multi: true
```

## Components

```mdl
component AnimatorArticle
  desc: >
    Article surface for an Animation. The stage of the current shot fills the article; below it the timeline from
    `@dxos/react-ui-animation` shows the shot list, per-shot track rows with key diamonds, effect rows and the
    script's beats, with play, scrub and timecode. The toolbar adds a shot, adds an effect and exports.
  props:
    role: string
    attendableId: string
    subject: Animation
  state:
    shot: string                    # current shot id
    time: number                    # clock time within the animation
    playing: boolean
  actions:
    play()
    pause()
    seek(t: number)
    addShot(stage: Ref<Obj.Unknown>)
    addEffect(effect: Ref<Effect>)
    export()
  layout: |
    ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │ [+ Shot][+ Effect][Export]                [⋮] │
    ├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ stage (contributed by the shot's plugin)     │
    ├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │ ▶ 00:12.40  shots | tracks ◆ | effects | beats│
    └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Operations

```mdl
op CreateAnimation
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.createAnimation
  desc: Creates an Animation with one shot per given stage object, each with an empty timeline.
  input:
    name?: string
    stages: Ref<Obj.Unknown>[]
    fps?: number
    target: Database | Collection
  output: Ref<Animation>
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SetKey
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.setKey
  desc: Keys a target property, an effect parameter or the camera at a time in a shot.
  input:
    animation: Ref<Animation>
    shot: string
    t: number
    path: string                    # `${target}:${property}`, `effect:${id}:${param}` or `camera:${property}`
    value: unknown
    ease?: Easing
  output: Ref<Animation>
  errors:
    UnknownTargetError: the stage does not list the target or the property is not animatable
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SetScript
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.setScript
  desc: Replaces a shot's script and compiles it to keys, returning compile errors by beat.
  input:
    animation: Ref<Animation>
    shot: string
    script: Beat[]
  output: Ref<Animation>
  errors:
    ScriptError: a beat names an unknown target, layout or effect
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op CreateEffect
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.effect.create
  desc: Writes a new Effect's source and parameter schema, compiles it, and returns compile errors.
  input:
    name: string
    description: string
    renderer: 2d | 3d | overlay
    source: string
    params: JsonSchema
    target: Database | Collection
  output: Ref<Effect>
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op UpdateEffect
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.effect.update
  desc: Replaces an Effect's source or schema, bumps its version, recompiles, and returns compile errors.
  input:
    effect: Ref<Effect>
    source?: string
    params?: JsonSchema
  output: Ref<Effect>
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op CheckEffect
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.effect.check
  desc: >
    Runs an Effect headless over a duration with given parameters; returns step timings, a determinism check (the
    same time reached from two checkpoints) and a contact sheet of frames.
  input:
    effect: Ref<Effect>
    params: Record<string, unknown>
    duration: number
  output: EffectReport
  effects: [echo:read]
```

```mdl
op PlaceEffect
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.effect.place
  desc: Adds an Effect to a shot with parameters and bindings to the shot's targets.
  input:
    animation: Ref<Animation>
    shot: string
    effect: Ref<Effect>
    params: Record<string, unknown>
    seed?: number
  output: Ref<Animation>
  errors:
    RendererError: the shot's stage cannot draw the effect's renderer
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op Render
  key: org.dxos.operation.animator.render
  desc: >
    Renders a time range of an Animation to H.264 MP4 and records it as a `video/mp4` Variant on a MediaArtifact
    with the request, so it can be re-rendered. Runs in the app by default and on EDGE when `where` is `edge`.
  input:
    animation: Ref<Animation>
    from?: number
    to?: number
    fps?: number
    size?: Size
    where?: app | edge
  output: Ref<Variant>
  effects: [echo:write]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Neutral animation core

  req F-1.1: Timelines, keys, easing, interpolation, the clock and the effect runtime live in `@dxos/animation`, and the timeline UI and clock hooks in `@dxos/react-ui-animation`; neither depends on any plugin.
  req F-1.2: react-ui-canvas imports both packages and keeps no copy or re-export of what moved.
  req F-1.3: `AnimatableAnnotation` is a serializable ECHO annotation recording an `AnimatableKind`, so it survives stored and dynamic schemas.
  req F-1.4: `animatableProperties(schema)` lists the keyable property paths and kinds of any schema, including one the animator has never seen.
  req F-1.5: Each `AnimatableKind` interpolates as its type states: `vec3` per axis, `rotation` by slerp, `color` in OKLab, `discrete` held.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Animations and shots

  req F-2.1: An Animation is an ECHO object whose shots reference stage objects; playing it never writes to those objects.
  req F-2.2: Shots play in order, each for its duration, joined by its transition.
  req F-2.3: Every canvas animation is an Animation; canvas documents hold no timeline of their own.
  req F-2.4: A track target is a stage-local id that the stage resolves; the animator stores it opaquely.
  req F-2.5: Editing a stage property at a time other than the shot's start writes a key at that time.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Declarative scripts

  req F-3.1: A shot's script compiles to keys; the same script and stage objects always produce the same keys.
  req F-3.2: Where a hand key and a compiled key set the same property at the same time, the hand key wins.
  req F-3.3: A beat's `layout` is computed by an arranger the stage contributes; the script never holds positions it did not set explicitly.
  req F-3.4: A script that names an unknown target, layout or effect fails to compile with an error naming the beat.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Stages

  req F-4.1: A plugin becomes animatable by contributing an `AnimatorCapabilities.Stage`; the animator holds no knowledge of its object model.
  req F-4.2: The canvas stage renders `Drawing.Canvas` scenes with a 2D pan and zoom camera and draws `2d` and `overlay` effects.
  req F-4.3: The spacetime stage renders `Spacetime.Scene` with Babylon.js and an orbit camera, and draws `3d` and `overlay` effects.
  req F-4.4: Every 3D stage uses Babylon.js.
  req F-4.5: The spacetime stage offers a presentation material for primitives (lit sphere with a rim glow, dithered so gradients do not band) and a lattice background, alongside its CAD materials.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Effects

  req F-5.1: An effect runs in a worker with no DOM, network or space access, under a per-step budget.
  req F-5.2: An effect's output is a pure function of time, parameters, bindings and seed; reaching a time from any checkpoint gives the same frame.
  req F-5.3: Effects do not read live ECHO data.
  req F-5.4: `3d` effects return instance lists, which the stage draws with instanced meshes; they own no Babylon nodes.
  req F-5.5: Numeric effect parameters are animatable on the shot's timeline.
  req F-5.6: Packet flow, burst, conversations and merge ship as built-in effects.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Playback and export

  req F-6.1: The animator owns the clock; no stage or effect reads wall-clock time.
  req F-6.2: Export sets the clock to `n / fps` for each frame and captures it only after the stage reports `onFrameDrawn` for that time.
  req F-6.3: Export runs in the app with WebCodecs by default, needing no native dependency.
  req F-6.4: Long renders run on EDGE in the existing sandbox containers, with progress reported and the result stored as a blob.
  req F-6.5: A local CLI renders an Animation by DXN for CI and development.
  req F-6.6: Encoding settings preserve the stage's dither so gradients do not band.
  req F-6.7: The animator renders picture only; audio is composed in plugin-studio.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: plugin-studio

  req F-7.1: The animator contributes a studio `GenerationService` provider of kind `video` whose result is a `video/mp4` Variant.
  req F-7.2: A long render uses studio's enqueue and await with a persisted job id, so it survives a reload.
  req F-7.3: A Variant of type `application/vnd.dxos.animation` plays the Animation live in studio before it is rendered.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Text and overlays

  req F-8.1: A stage draws a label beside each target that has one, in a style the shot sets per target (`hero`, `title`, `inside`, plain) or hides; labels fade with their target.
  req F-8.2: A label's text is animatable as `discrete`, and a change of text can morph by sliding the words that differ.
  req F-8.3: A shot shows screen text above the stage on the timeline: captions with staggered lines, a side title, an image headline, and a full-frame curtain that fades to a colour and back.
  req F-8.4: Callout panels and message threads anchored to targets are an `overlay` effect.
  req F-8.5: Screen text is drawn by the animator, not the stage, so every stage gets it.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Canvas animation is unchanged by the extraction
  given: the canvas generator tests and stories from before the extraction
  then: they pass with react-ui-canvas importing `@dxos/animation`
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A film across two canvas scenes
  given: two canvas drawings
  when:
    - CreateAnimation over both
    - Key a node's position in the first shot and SetScript a show-and-layout beat in the second
  then:
    - playback runs both shots in order
    - neither drawing changed in ECHO
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Deterministic effects
  given: each built-in effect with fixed parameters and seed
  then: CheckEffect reports the same frame for the same time from two checkpoints
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: The echo3d story as an Animation
  given: spacetime scenes holding the echo3d presentation's objects
  then:
    - an Animation scripted from its scenes plays with packet flow, burst, conversations and merge
    - its labels, captions, curtain, panels and sphere look match the echo3d video, apart from sound
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Export matches playback
  given: an Animation with a camera move and an effect
  when: Render two seconds at 60 fps in the app
  then:
    - the MP4 has 120 frames and lands as a `video/mp4` Variant
    - each frame matches the live frame sampled at the same time
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: A new plugin, plugin-animator, provides 2D and 3D animation; the animation engine is plugin-neutral, factored out of plugin-canvas's animation rather than written anew.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Animations have timeline controls, and are made of scenes that reference objects whose parameters are set or tweened at key points.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Animation, Shot, F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: The plugins that own the target objects provide the objects and their renderer, and object schemas mark the properties that can be tweened.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [AnimatorCapabilities.Stage, AnimatableKind, F-1.3, F-4]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Custom objects are generated code that performs effects, such as data communication and particles.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Effect, F-5]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: An animation renders locally or on EDGE, and the result can be included as a plugin-studio clip.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6, F-7]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: Every canvas animation is an Animation; canvas documents have no separate timeline. No migration is needed because canvas animation has not shipped.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2.3]
  why: Canvas animation has not shipped, so there is no stored data to migrate.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: 3D stages use Babylon.js only; there is no Three.js stage.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-4.3, F-4.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Shots can be authored declaratively, as scene states compiled to keys, from the first version.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Beat, F-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-9: `3d` effects return instance lists; effects that own Babylon nodes are deferred.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-10: EDGE renders run in the existing sandbox containers before any dedicated media service is considered.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Effects are purely visual and do not read live ECHO data.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-5.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Audio stays in plugin-studio and is not placed on the animator timeline.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-6.7]
```

```mdl
decision D-13: The neutral core is two packages, `@dxos/animation` (model, clock, script compiler, effect runtime) and `@dxos/react-ui-animation` (timeline UI, clock hooks), moved out of react-ui-canvas with no re-exports. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1.1, F-1.2]
  why: The canvas engine already works; moving it keeps canvas behaviour and avoids a second engine. Splitting UI from model keeps the model usable headless (export, EDGE).
  rejected:
    - One package: forces React on headless renderers.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: An Animation is its own ECHO object made of shots, each referencing one stage object, and playback never writes to the referenced objects. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Animation, Shot, F-2.1, F-2.2, F-2.4]
  why: A film can span objects from several plugins, and one object can appear in several films without being edited.
  rejected:
    - Timeline data inside each plugin's document: cannot span plugins.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Stage plugins contribute an `AnimatorCapabilities.Stage` that lists targets and properties, renders a `Sample` and `EffectFrame`s, and reports `onFrameDrawn`; the animatable marker is a serializable `Annotation.make` annotation recording an `AnimatableKind`. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [AnimatorCapabilities.Stage, AnimatableKind, F-1.3, F-1.4, F-1.5, F-4.1, F-6.2]
  why: The raw annotation key in react-ui-canvas does not survive stored schemas; the frame handshake makes export capture the frame that was asked for.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: Effects generalise canvas generators: one sandboxed, seeded, checkpointed runtime with three renderers (`2d`, `3d`, `overlay`), animatable numeric parameters, and packet flow, burst, conversations and merge ported from echo3d as built-ins. Fills in [D-4].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Effect, EffectInstance, EffectFrame, F-5.1, F-5.2, F-5.5, F-5.6]
  why: One sandbox and one determinism contract serve every renderer, and the generator runtime already provides them.
```

```mdl
decision D-17: Export runs in the app with WebCodecs by default, on EDGE for long renders, and through a local CLI for CI, all driven by the animator's clock. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [op:Render, F-6.1, F-6.2, F-6.3, F-6.5, F-6.6]
  why: WebCodecs needs no native dependency in the browser or the desktop webview; EDGE takes renders too long for a tab.
  rejected:
    - A native desktop sidecar: only worth adding if WebCodecs proves too slow.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: A rendered animation reaches plugin-studio through a `GenerationService` provider of kind `video` producing a `video/mp4` Variant, and a live `application/vnd.dxos.animation` Variant previews it before rendering. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-7]
  why: Studio already models clips as Variants and long jobs as enqueue and await with a persisted job id.
```

```mdl
decision D-19: A script is a list of beats (show, hide, set, layout, merge, camera, effects, caption); layouts come from arrangers the stage contributes, and hand keys win over compiled keys. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Beat, op:SetScript, F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.3, F-3.4]
  why: The beat shape is the one echo3d's views proved over 28 slides; letting hand keys win keeps fine adjustments when a script is recompiled.
```

```mdl
decision D-20: Phase 3 reproduces the echo3d presentation's look as well as its motion: on-screen text (labels, captions, title cards, the curtain), callout panels, and a presentation material in the spacetime stage, so the rebuilt video matches the original apart from sound.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-4.5, F-8]
```

```mdl
decision D-21: Screen text (captions, side title, image headline, curtain) belongs to the animator and draws above any stage, while target labels belong to the stage and panels are an overlay effect. Fills in [D-20].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-8.1, F-8.3, F-8.4, F-8.5]
  why: Screen text is independent of the object model, so one implementation serves every stage; labels need the stage's projection; panels follow targets as effects already do.
  rejected:
    - All text as overlay effects: captions would need bindings they do not use.
```

---

```mdl
decision D-22: The implemented operation keys take the repository's `<root>.operation.<package>.<verbNoun>` shape: `animator.createAnimation`, `animator.setKey` (the `Key` operation renamed `SetKey`) and `animator.setScript`. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [op:CreateAnimation, op:SetKey, op:SetScript]
  why: The `operation-key-shape` lint rule rejects dotted subject paths such as `animator.timeline.key`, and a red lint fails CI.
  rejected: Keeping the dotted keys and disabling the rule for this package.
```

```mdl
decision D-23: A stage target carries its resting values, which a script compiles from, and a stage reports an edit made at the sample's time through an `onEdit` callback, which the animator writes as keys on the shot. Fills in [D-15].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [AnimatorCapabilities.Stage, F-2.5, F-3.1]
  why: A script states targets' end states, so the compiler needs where each starts; keeping the write in the animator leaves the stage unable to write a timeline it does not own.
  rejected: A separate `values(stage)` function on the stage, which would read the stage object twice.
```

```mdl
decision D-24: The canvas stage receives each sample as held keys on its scene engine's animated projection, and a canvas View holds no timeline: the engine takes the timeline from its host, and composite objects carry no animation of their own. Fills in [D-6].
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-2.3, F-4.2]
  why: Reusing the animated projection keeps hit testing, generators and the camera drawing the sampled scene without a second sampling path.
  rejected: Keeping `View.timeline` beside `Animation` as a second place animation lives.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap
    literals?: UnionList
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext capability
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.capability@1.0
  desc: |
    A typed slot in the app-framework Capability registry. Single-instance
    by default; `multi: true` marks contributable collections.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    type: TypeRef
    events?: EventList
    multi?: boolean
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap
    state?: FieldMap
    slots?: FieldMap
    actions?: ActionMap
    emits?: EventMap
    layout?: CodeBlock
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1
  desc: A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
  fields:
    key?: NSID
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap
    output?: TypeExpr
    errors?: ErrorMap
    effects?: EffectList
    requires?: ServiceList
    note?: Prose
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

`decision` is defined in `org.dxos.spec.changelog`.
